    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Frequent molecular alterations in uterine leiomyoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 703.3pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Frequency</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Target(s)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.65pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"397\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Mechanisms</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 221.35pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"295\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>References</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">70%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>MED12</em> (Xq13.1)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"397\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Exon&nbsp;2 mutations</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 221.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"295\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{21868628; 22768200; 26037152; 22428002; 22532225; 27363490; 29666002; 27187686; 28592321}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">25&ndash;29%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>HMGA2</em> (12q15) and <em>HMGA1</em> (6p21.31)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"397\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Multiple fusion transcripts, commonly <em>HMGA2</em>-<em>RAD51B</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 221.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"295\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{30292626; 26787895; 28592321}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">4%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>COL4A5</em> and <em>COL4A6</em> (Xq22)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"397\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Somatic or germline X-linked dominant Xq22 deletion (Alport syndrome&nbsp;/ diffuse leiomyomatosis)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 221.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"295\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{26787895; 10730274}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">1%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>FH</em> (1q43)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.65pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"397\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Somatic (1q43 deletion, mutation, and biallelic inactivation) or germline autosomal dominant 1q43 mutation (hereditary leiomyomatosis and renal cell carcinoma)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 221.35pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"295\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{28863073; 28664937; 27363490; 11248088; 27187686; 26574848; 26787895; 28592321}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 36597,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 237,
    "fileId": 10818,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria for leiomyoma and subtypes</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 53.4pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 53.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Usual-type leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Intersecting fascicles of spindle cells with eosinophilic fibrillary cytoplasm and cigar-shaped nuclei lacking cytological atypia; very low mitotic count</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.8pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.8pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Cellular leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">More cellular than the surrounding myometrium; thick-walled vessels and cleft-like spaces; cells have scant cytoplasm</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 53.4pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 53.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Leiomyoma with bizarre nuclei</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Bizarre cells in a background of typical leiomyoma; low mitotic count (&lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup>, equating to &lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;HPF of 0.55&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.24 mm<sup>2</sup> in area)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 39.6pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.6pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Fumarate hydratase&ndash;deficient leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Staghorn vessels; alveolar-type oedema; may have cells with bizarre nuclei; large nuclei with perinucleolar haloes; rhabdoid inclusions</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Mitotically active leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Leiomyoma with 2.5&ndash;6&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (equating to 6&ndash;14&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;HPF of 0.55&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.24 mm<sup>2</sup> in area); no cytological atypia</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 39.6pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.6pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Hydropic leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Prominent oedematous stroma that causes compartmentalization of the smooth muscle cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 39.6pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.6pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Apoplectic leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Stellate zones of haemorrhage; zonation phenomenon; history of progestogen treatment or pregnancy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 39.6pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.6pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lipoleiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Admixture of mature adipocytes and smooth muscle cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 53.4pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 53.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Epithelioid leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rounded or polygonal cells with eosinophilic granular or clear cytoplasm; no cytological atypia; &lt;&nbsp;0.8&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (equating to &lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;HPF of 0.55&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.24 mm<sup>2</sup> in area)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 39.6pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.6pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Myxoid leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Circumscribed, hypocellular and myxoid tumour lacking cytological atypia or mitoses</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 39.6pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.6pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Cotyledonoid dissecting leiomyoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Irregular nodular dissection of bland smooth muscle cells within the myometrium</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 39.6pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 688.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 39.6pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Diffuse leiomyomatosis</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Innumerable, poorly circumscribed hypercellular tumour nodules with no cytological atypia within the myometrium</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
